      "date": "1970-07-16",
      "kind": "planning decision",
      "description": "A building on the 60,600-square-foot lot housed the headquarters of the Fire Department's Bureau of Engineering and Water Supply, with pipe storage at the rear. The City Planning Commission found the transfer of this lot from the Department of Public Works to the Fire Department in conformity with the Master Plan, clearing the way for a new firehouse for Engine Company 37 and Truck Company 9, moved from 25th and Vermont Streets.",
